From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:15:00 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] atari-core-tests

Stella 2014 (Atari 2600) and ProSystem (Atari 7800) run on the generic
libretro host before any Atari platform code exists, with no BIOS.

2600: a generated 4 KB VSYNC kernel cart draws 160x210 at 59.92 fps with
31400 Hz sound (524 samples a frame) and a tone; a 312-line one is PAL,
160x250 at 49.92 fps. States round-trip, there is no save RAM. The
difficulty switches latch (L and R set A, L2 and R2 set B), so do Colour
and Black/White (L3, R3); SELECT and START (Reset) count only while held;
fire is RetroPad B.

7800: a generated 16 KB cart draws its background at 320x223 and 60 fps
(31440 Hz, 524 samples), or 320x272 at 50 fps when its header says PAL;
a headerless dump the core's database does not know runs as NTSC. States
round-trip, there is no save RAM, and every console switch, difficulty
included, counts only while held. With SLOT_7800_BIOS pointing at the
NTSC BIOS the same unsigned cart never draws; without the variable that
test prints a BIOS skip.

The 2600 cart has the shape of the ROM in stella2014's own
test/determinism_harness.c; the code and the checks are new.
